   "rawText": "Additional Courses: Require a grade of C or better\nSelect 3-4 credits in Statistics:3-4\nSTAT 100Statistical Concepts and Reasoning\nSTAT 200Elementary Statistics\nSTAT 240Introduction to Biometry\nSTAT 250Introduction to Biostatistics\nSTAT 401Experimental Methods\nSelect 3-4 credits in Mathematics (MATH 33 preferred):3-4\nMATH 21College Algebra with Analytic Geometry with Applications I\nMATH 22College Algebra With Analytic Geometry and Applications II\nMATH 26Plane Trigonometry and Applications of Trigonometry\nMATH 33Mathematics for Sustainability (preferred)\nMATH 34The Mathematics of Money\nMATH 35General View of Mathematics\nMATH 36Insights Into Mathematics\nMATH 37Finite Mathematics\nMATH 38Elementary Linear Algebra\nMATH 41Trigonometry and Analytic Geometry\nMATH 81Technical Mathematics I\nMATH 82Technical Mathematics II\nMATH 83Technical Calculus\nMATH 110Techniques of Calculus I\nMATH 140Calculus With Analytic Geometry I\nMATH 140GCalculus with Earth and Mineral Sciences Applications I\nMATH 140HHonors Calculus with Analytic Geometry I\nMATH 141Calculus with Analytic Geometry II\nMATH 141GCalculus with Earth and Mineral Sciences Applications II\nMATH 141HHonors Calculus with Analytic Geometry II\nSelect 3 credits in Engaged Scholarship:3\nEMSC 299Foreign Studies\nEMSC 470WUndergraduate Collaborative Research in Earth and Materials Sciences\nGEOG 199Foreign Studies\nGEOG 294Research Project\nGEOG 296Independent Studies\nGEOG 299Foreign Studies\nGEOG 399Foreign Studies\nGEOG 493Service Learning\nGEOG 494Research Project in Geography\nGEOG 494HResearch Project in Geography\nGEOG 495Internship\nGEOG 495BGeography Teaching Internship\nGEOG 496Independent Studies\nGEOG 499Foreign Studies\nSelect 3 credits of 300-level Geography: 3\nGEOG 310Introduction to Global Climatic Systems\nGEOG 314Biogeography and Global Ecology\nGEOG 320Fundamentals of Urban Geography\nGEOG 324Place, Space and Culture\nGEOG 326Geographies of the Economy: Power and Place\nGEOG 328War, Peace, and Diplomacy: Understanding Contemporary Geopolitics\nGEOG 330NPolitical Ecology\nSelect 12 credits of 400-level Geography:12\nGEOG 414Principles and Applications in Landscape Ecology\nGEOG 420YComparative Urbanism\nGEOG 424WGeography of the Global Economy\nGEOG 426WGendered Worlds\nGEOG 428WPolitical Geography\nGEOG 430Human Use of Environment\nGEOG 431Geography of Water Resources\nGEOG 432Energy Policy\nGEOG 433Geographies of Justice\nGEOG 434Politics of the Environment\nGEOG 437WEnergy Geographies and Policy\nGEOG 438WHuman Dimensions of a Changing Climate\nGEOG/AFR 444Resource Governance in Africa\n"
